false_positives.candidate:
No tests cover logging in or disabling 2FA with a backup code

The new authentication paths are untested end to end:
- backup-code login in `authorize`;
- consumption of a used code, so reuse must fail;
- disabling 2FA with a backup code.

The PR only exercises the download and copy buttons and leaves a TODO. The existing assertion `expect(page.locator(...).isChecked()).toBeTruthy()` checks a Promise and is always truthy, as the added FIXME admits. These are security-relevant flows and should have coverage before merging.

true_positives.matched_candidate:
Client removal no longer cleans up V2 permissions; V1+V2 combination throws on delete

The listener now only runs when V1 `ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ` is enabled. Under V2 nothing cleans up when a client is deleted:
- the per-client resource (named after the client id) stays in the admin-permissions client;
- scope permissions referencing that resource stay as well;
- those permissions keep pointing at a non-existent client.

If V1 and V2 are both enabled, `management()` returns `MgmtPermissionsV2`. Its `clients().setPermissionsEnabled` throws `UnsupportedOperationException`, so deleting a client would fail.

false_positives.candidate:
No test that legitimate HTML/anchors pass without errors

All the new tests only check that violations are reported. None checks that valid input produces no messages, for example:
- an identical anchor in the translation;
- allowed tags like `<br />` or `<b>` when the English value has HTML;
- entities like `&laquo;`;
- `{{x}}` placeholders.

The verifier's unescape and comment-stripping normalization is fragile. Without negative tests, false positives that break the build would go unnoticed.

